  ("Why did Hari Singh decide to return to Anil?", "He remembered that education could make him a respected man, and he understood that Anil's trust meant more than a few hundred rupees. He went back to learn to read and write."),
  ("What was Anil's reaction when he found the money returned?", "He did not say anything. He made tea, gave Hari a fifty-rupee note and promised regular pay and lessons in sentences."),
  ("How does the story show that Anil is different from other employers?", "He trusts his servant, gives him a key, teaches him, and does not punish or call the police when he realises the theft."),
  ("What is the significance of the wet note?", "It proves that Anil found and kept the returned money, which was damp from the rain, and that he knew about the theft."),
